Here is the structured goal model for the multi-robot food delivery and dish retrieval system:

### Goal Model

| Goal ID | Goal Title                 | Text                                                         | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G1      | Deliver Food and Retrieve Dishes | Ensure food is delivered and dishes are retrieved successfully. | -                  | Achieve   | -        |
| G2      | Food Delivery              | Successfully deliver food to the inpatient room.             | ;                  | Perform   | G1       |
| G3      | Dish Retrieval             | Successfully retrieve dirty dishes from the inpatient room.    | ;                  | Perform   | G1       |

### Sub-Goals and Tasks

#### Food Delivery (G2)
| Goal ID | Goal Title                 | Text                                                         | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G2.1    | Move to Kitchen           | Navigate to the kitchen area.                                 | -                  | Perform   | G2       |
| G2.2    | Deliver Food to Room      | Place food on the room table or hand it over.                 | -                  | Perform   | G2       |
| G2.3    | Return to Kitchen         | Navigate back to the kitchen after delivery.                  | -                  | Perform   | G2       |

#### Dish Retrieval (G3)
| Goal ID | Goal Title                 | Text                                                         | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G3.1    | Move to Patient Room      | Navigate to the specified patient room.                       | -                  | Perform   | G3       |
| G3.2    | Retrieve Dishes           | Collect dirty dishes from the room.                           | -                  | Perform   | G3       |
| G3.3    | Return to Kitchen         | Navigate back to the kitchen after retrieval.                 | -                  | Perform   | G3       |

### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title             | Text                                           | Relation | Location          | Number of Robots |
| ------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------- | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Move to Kitchen        | Navigate to the kitchen area.                  | AND      | Kitchen           | 1                |
| AT2     | Deliver Food           | Place food on the room table or hand it over. | AND      | Patient Room      | 1                |
| AT3     | Return from Kitchen    | Navigate back to the kitchen.                 | AND      | Kitchen           | 1                |
| AT4     | Move to Patient Room   | Navigate to the specified patient room.        | AND      | Patient Room      | 1                |
| AT5     | Retrieve Dishes        | Collect dirty dishes from the room.            | AND      | Patient Room      | 1                |
| AT6     | Return to Kitchen      | Navigate back to the kitchen.                 | AND      | Kitchen           | 1                |

### Justifications

- **G1 Relation (AND)**: Both food delivery and dish retrieval must succeed for the mission to be complete.
- **G2 and G3 Relations (AND)**: Each sub-goal must be completed in sequence for the parent goal to succeed.
- **Tasks Relation (AND)**: Each task within a sub-goal must be executed in sequence, requiring one robot each time.

This model ensures that each step is executed in the correct order, with each task handled by a single robot, ensuring efficient and reliable delivery and retrieval processes.
